        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram-miniapp): cancel unread response body on auth error",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen the Telegram Mini App page receives a non-ok HTTP response (e.g., 401 auth error), the response body stream is left dangling without being cancelled. This can leak connections and waste resources.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe established codebase pattern is to cancel the response body before throwing on non-ok responses (see `extensions/chutes/oauth.ts`, `extensions/openrouter/usage.ts`, etc.). This fix applies the same pattern to the Telegram Mini App page handler.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Resources are cleaned up immediately on auth error instead of dangling until garbage collection.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Tests**: 2/2 passed (page.test.ts)\n- **Body cancel behavior verified**: Body cancelled on auth error, cancel rejection doesn't mask original error, null body safe\n- **Pattern**: `await response.body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined)` — matches codebase convention\n\n```\n Body cancel on auth error ---\n Body cancelled: YES\n Error: Telegram Mini App auth failed (401)\n\n Cancel rejection -> original error preserved ---\n Cancel rejection handled: YES\n Error: Authentication error: invalid init data\n\n Null body handling ---\n Null body safe: YES\n Error: Auth failed\n```",
        "branch": "fix/telegram-miniapp-body-cancel",
